# DIAGNOSTICS

A failure at start prints `drv-virtio-net: FAILED:` and what failed, and exits with that: `no listen channel`, `no configuration space or DMA domain`, `no MSIs`, `not a modern virtio device with MSI-X`, `feature negotiation`, `the queues`, `no memory for buffers` or `port_create`.
It exits `the listen channel is gone` if its post's listen end closes.

# BUGS

One card: a second has no post of its own.
One client, so only netd can use the card.
No offloads: no checksum offload, segmentation or merged receive buffers, and the device's own MTU and link status are not read; the MTU is always 1500.
Every frame is copied, once each way, between the device's buffers and the session's arenas.
The legacy and transitional devices (1af4:1000) are not matched.
